CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ one argument passed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Declaring a function template recorded each of its parameter packs as
empty in the global template map and never removed the entry; the
trailing return type of call() then expanded `args...' as that empty
pack, `c()' had too few arguments and call had no viable candidate.
